[HEADING=1]XenForo 2.3.13 — PHP 8.2 → 8.6 Web Stack Benchmark[/HEADING]

[I]Part 1 of 2 — setup and per-host results[/I]

[HEADING=2]TL;DR[/HEADING]

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Question[/TH][TH]Answer[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]Biggest performance win[/TD][TD][B]Angie [ICODE]fastcgi_cache[/ICODE] guest-page cache[/B]: [B]88×–180×[/B] more guest requests/s[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Fastest stack overall[/TD][TD][B]Stack 3 — Valkey + Angie page cache[/B] (guest-heavy forum)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Fastest stack for logged-in users[/TD][TD][B]Stack 1 — plain Angie + PHP + MariaDB[/B] (no Valkey, no page cache)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Does Valkey data caching help a single server?[/TD][TD][B]No.[/B] It costs [B]2–14 %[/B] versus plain; Credis and phpredis measured the same[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Cost of Anubis[/TD][TD][B]−90…−94 %[/B] on cached guest pages, [B]−17…−19 %[/B] on dynamic/member pages[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]PHP 8.6 vs 8.2[/TD][TD][B]+0…+3 %[/B] at low concurrency; [B]≤1.5 %[/B] at saturation — no meaningful gain[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]PHP version ranking[/TD][TD][B]8.6 RC5 > 8.5 > 8.4 ≈ 8.2 > 8.3[/B] (differences are small)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]PHP 8.6 without [ICODE]php-redis[/ICODE][/TD][TD]Works with [B]SV/RedisCache + bundled Credis[/B]; all add-ons active, all tiers HTTP 200[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

[HEADING=2]Test environment[/HEADING]

[HEADING=3]Hardware[/HEADING]

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Spec[/TH][TH]Host A (remote)[/TH][TH]Host B (local)[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]CPU[/TD][TD]AMD EPYC 4245P, [B]6 cores / 12 threads[/B], 5.49 GHz max[/TD][TD]AMD Ryzen 7 8745HS, [B]8 cores / 16 threads[/B], 4.97 GHz max[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]RAM[/TD][TD]30 GiB[/TD][TD]27 GiB[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Disk[/TD][TD]2× 894 GB Samsung NVMe[/TD][TD]931 GB Crucial NVMe[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Virtualisation[/TD][TD]none detected ([ICODE]systemd-detect-virt[/ICODE])[/TD][TD]none detected[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]OS[/TD][TD]Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS[/TD][TD]Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Kernel[/TD][TD]7.0.0-43-generic[/TD][TD]7.0.0-43-generic[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

[HEADING=3]Software[/HEADING]

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Component[/TH][TH]Version[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]Angie[/TD][TD]1.12.4[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]PHP[/TD][TD]8.2.35, 8.3.36, 8.4.27, 8.5.12, [B]8.6.0RC5[/B] (Sury packages, side by side)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]MariaDB[/TD][TD]11.8.6[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Valkey[/TD][TD]9.0.4[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Anubis[/TD][TD]1.28.2 (opt-in, stack 4 only)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]XenForo[/TD][TD]2.3.13[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Add-ons[/TD][TD]SV/StandardLib 1.24.11, SV/RedisCache 2.18.12, SV/RedisFloodCheck 2.3.1, SV/RedisViewCounter 2.6.2, Hampel/Seeder 1.0.0b11[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Load generator[/TD][TD]wrk 4.1.0 (loopback, HTTPS)[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

[B]Redis client:[/B] [ICODE]php-redis[/ICODE] is [B]not installed on any PHP version[/B]. SV/RedisCache uses its bundled pure-PHP [B]Credis[/B] client on 8.2–8.6. A separate control showed phpredis and Credis within 1–2 % of each other on this workload, so the PHP-version comparison is like for like.

[B]PHP profile:[/B] [ICODE]pm = static[/ICODE], 12 workers (Host A) / 16 workers (Host B), [ICODE]memory_limit=512M[/ICODE], OPcache 512 MB, interned strings 64 MB, [B]JIT tracing, 64 MB[/B], hot thresholds [ICODE]64/127/16/64[/ICODE]. JIT was confirmed active on every version.

[B]Rate limiting:[/B] all Angie [ICODE]limit_req[/ICODE] directives were disabled for the tests.

[HEADING=2]Dataset[/HEADING]

Seeded with the [B]Hampel Seeder[/B] add-on:

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Content[/TH][TH]Count[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]Users[/TD][TD][B]20,001[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Threads[/TD][TD][B]10,000[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Posts[/TD][TD][B]100,400[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Forum nodes[/TD][TD][B]47[/B] (categories, forums, sub-forums)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Timespan[/TD][TD]2 years[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

Member account used for logged-in tests: [ICODE]meta.johns[/ICODE] (valid, normal registered user).

[HEADING=2]Method[/HEADING]

[LIST]
[*]Loopback HTTPS against [ICODE]xf.test.local[/ICODE], self-signed certificate.
[*][ICODE]wrk -t4 -c100 -d10s[/ICODE], 2 s warm-up, per tier.
[*][B]Guest cached:[/B] [ICODE]GET /[/ICODE] with no cookies.
[*][B]Guest bypass:[/B] [ICODE]GET /[/ICODE] with [ICODE]Cookie: xf_session=bench-bypass[/ICODE] (bypasses the guest cache without logging in).
[*][B]Member home:[/B] [ICODE]GET /[/ICODE] with a valid XenForo session cookie.
[*][B]Member thread:[/B] a seeded 100k-post thread with the same session cookie.
[*]The FastCGI cache was cleared before each PHP version; Valkey DB 1 was flushed when the data cache was toggled.
[*]The active PHP version was verified with a [ICODE]PHP_VERSION[/ICODE] probe on every run (the first attempt exposed a stale Anubis connection pool serving the previous PHP version; the final runs force a restart on version changes).
[*]Low-concurrency efficiency: [ICODE]wrk -t2 -c8 -d15s[/ICODE], [B]3 runs averaged[/B], plain stack.
[/LIST]

[QUOTE]The four stack passes ran sequentially. Small differences between Stack 1 and Stack 2 (a few percent) are within run-order/thermal drift; the page-cache and Anubis effects are far larger than that drift.[/QUOTE]

